# ProxyAPI adapter rules

- ProxyAPI integration exists only inside provider/infrastructure adapters.
- Never expose or log the ProxyAPI API key.
- Keep base URL/key/timeouts in validated server configuration; user input never controls provider host/base URL.
- Treat streams/responses as untrusted external data and validate financially important usage fields.
- Capture provider request IDs for support/reconciliation.
- Streaming parser must tolerate partial chunks, multiple events, terminal usage chunks with empty choices and unexpected EOF.
- Corporate ProxyAPI balance/key budget is treasury state, separate from user usage.
- Provider 402/budget failures are not user-insufficient-usage errors.
- Ambiguous timeouts/502/504/stream failures are not automatically safe to retry/release.
- Use separate dev/staging/prod keys, provider-side budget/model restrictions and IP restrictions when operationally available.
- Do not enable detailed prompt/response provider logging by default without explicit privacy/retention decision.
